  "preamble": "Retraction of [s] to the retroflex [ʂ]. The classic case is the Indo-Iranian ruki law: after r, u, k or i, PIE *s became a retracted sibilant, which is retroflex ṣ [ʂ] in Sanskrit, and the rule stayed active in Sanskrit sandhi.",
